  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 845742,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 'Nam 1965-1975: A Decade of Conflict on the Amiga\n\nStep into the tumultuous era of the Vietnam War in *'Nam 1965-1975*, a gripping wargame for the Commodore Amiga. Assume the weighty role of the US President and Commander-in-Chief, charged with preventing the collapse of South Vietnam against the rising tide of Communist forces. \n\nThis comprehensive simulation spans a decade, demanding you navigate a complex web of military strategy, economic policy, and public opinion.  Manage resources, deploy troops against both North Vietnamese regulars and elusive Viet Cong guerillas, and carefully consider the socio-political ramifications of your decisions.  Every action carries consequences – a misstep could lead to dwindling public support or even impeachment. \n\n*’Nam 1965-1975* offers a challenging and immersive experience, requiring astute planning and a deep understanding of the Vietnam War’s intricacies. Can you achieve victory and secure South Vietnam’s future, or will the conflict consume your presidency?"
    },
